From: mrdidit <26687854+mrdidit@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd939x: program Class-H transport fields

The Class-H sink implements the full data-port transport registers. Its
SIMPLE declaration skips OffsetCtrl2, BlockCtrl3, SampleCtrl2 and HCTRL,
leaving the codec window and packing inconsistent with the master setup.

Declare only the Class-H port FULL so the SoundWire core programs those
fields from the existing transport parameters. Keep channel preparation,
sample interval, channel mapping and the other ports unchanged.

Link: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/pull/803#issuecomment-6481609416
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
 	},
 	{
 		.num = WCD939X_CLSH_PORT,
-		.type = SDW_DPN_SIMPLE,
+		.type = SDW_DPN_FULL,
 		.min_ch = 1,
 		.max_ch = 1,
 		.simple_ch_prep_sm = true,
